# Dirty guard switch regression - 2026-07-01

Command:

```bash
npm test -- --run src/lib/fileActions.test.ts src/lib/openDocumentFlow.test.ts src/app/useAppFileActionsModel.test.tsx src/domains/document/components/DirtyDocumentSwitchModal.test.tsx
```

Result:

```text
Test Files  4 passed (4)
Tests       32 passed (32)
```

Coverage:

- Workspace navigation uses the current-window policy with `dirtyGuard: true`.
- Dirty switch prompt exposes save, save as, discard, and cancel actions.
- Cancel keeps the dirty current document and does not read the target file.
- Discard opens the target file without saving dirty edits.
- Save writes the current document before opening the target file.
- Save as requests a new path, writes dirty edits there, then opens the target file.
- External disk changes during save-before-switch keep the current document in conflict state.
